<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE NEGOTIATING ARC of the connect object (handoff §4, «Подключаемся — одна дуга по
  кругу, 1100 мс»), ported 1:1 from the prototype's own SVG:

      <svg viewBox="0 0 214 214" style="animation:spin 1100ms linear infinite">
        <circle cx="107" cy="107" r="85" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-dasharray="104 430" />

  Every number below is that line. The viewport is 214, i.e. @dimen/connect_object, so
  one viewport unit is one dp and the arc rides the ACTIVE ring exactly — inset 22 in a
  214 box is a circle of radius 85, which is the ring HomeFragment.buildConnectObject
  strokes at @dimen/stroke_emphasis. The stroke is that same 2.

  trimPathEnd is the dash: the circumference at r=85 is 534.07, the prototype shows 104
  of it, and 104/534.07 = 0.195. ONE arc and never a train of segments (§11 grabl 7).

  It is WHITE and tinted at the ImageView (`app:tint="?attr/colorAccentFigure"`), the
  same way @drawable/ic_flow_arc is tinted on the прогрузка ring — a vector cannot carry
  a theme attribute in strokeColor without forking this file per theme.

  The revolution is NOT here: it is one infinite ObjectAnimator on ROTATION at
  @integer/motion_spin, linear, started and stopped by HomeFragment. That is the route
  FlowOverlay.startArc already takes, and it is what finally lands §4's 1100 exactly —
  a Material CircularProgressIndicator owns its own clock and cannot be told this number.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="@dimen/connect_object"
    android:height="@dimen/connect_object"
    android:viewportWidth="214"
    android:viewportHeight="214">
    <path
        android:pathData="M107,22 A85,85 0 0,1 107,192 A85,85 0 0,1 107,22"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="2"
        android:trimPathEnd="0.195"
        android:trimPathStart="0" />
</vector>
